# Build context for docker/service.Dockerfile (see docs/adr/0014-container-images.md).
# Deny by default: only the files an image needs are sent to the Docker daemon, so a new local file
# (a secret, a data dump, a scratch script) can't end up in an image by accident.
*

# What the build uses: the workspace manifests and lockfile, each package's source, and the
# discovery watchlist (public configuration baked into that image).
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!libs/*/pyproject.toml
!libs/*/src
!services/*/pyproject.toml
!services/*/src
!config/watchlist.toml

# Never sent, even from inside the paths allowed above. Most are already excluded by `*`; they are
# listed so they stay excluded if the allowlist above ever widens.
**/.env
**/.env.*
.git
**/.venv
data
**/tests
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/node_modules
